# What must never be uploaded to a Vercel build.
#
# `vercel --prod` from a workstation uploads the WORKING TREE, not HEAD, so
# untracked files ride along unless they are listed here. On 2026-09-18 a
# working-tree deploy would have carried two MagTec employee census CSVs into
# the build; they were moved aside by hand that time. This file makes it
# automatic, because "someone remembers to move the file" is not a control.
#
# Vercel reads this file INSTEAD of .gitignore when it is present, so it has to
# list the build-irrelevant heavy directories too, not just the extras.

# ── Dependencies and build output ───────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules
.next
out
build
coverage
.vercel
.git

# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.pem

# ── Client and employee data ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing in the app is built from a spreadsheet: no CSV or workbook is tracked
# in this repo, so excluding the whole class costs the build nothing and stops
# a census export or a roster reconciliation from being uploaded.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xlsx
*.xls

# ── Client documents ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Controlled documents belonging to the client. The repo carries the decks
# derived from them, never the documents themselves.
*.docx
*.pptx
Brians Revisions/
Kenai-SOPs/

# ── Local artifacts that are not part of the app ────────────────────────────
# One-off migration and patch scripts kept beside the project, plus zipped
# snapshots. app-audit.zip is why *.zip is here: a zipped copy of the app
# carried the client export credentials into a public repository.
*.zip
*.py
run-the-job.html
deno.lock
supabase/.temp/
tha_results.txt

# ── Supabase Edge Functions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deployed with `supabase functions deploy`, never built by Next.js.
supabase/functions/
